{"baseRefOid":"815bb82b8103c88ef6ba50620128780c9d64b216","body":"Native interactions could lose focus across repaint, virtual scrolling could invalidate visible rows or retain removed resources, and Canvas padding/border made rotation and hit testing disagree with actual paint. This change makes retained identity, full virtual targets and measured Canvas drawable geometry authoritative across those paths.\n\nVirtual target commits retain old state/recipes/resources, execute new rows and release removed rows together, with rollback of failed candidates. Seed and delayed row callbacks and read dependencies preserve their real executable owner. Accepting drop targets determine scroll ancestry; a validated unoccluded destination may continue across row gaps, using bounded native ticks after presentation. Cancelled effect deliveries and completed wheel sessions release callback/Escape authority correctly.\n\nAlso corrects RangeSlider endpoints, Table local rollback, online diagnostic bounds, negative collection budgets and Tree indexing. Invalid state defaults now report their field path, with recursive tagged-value examples in USER_GUIDE.\n\nCloses #93\n\nValidation:\n\n- historical adversarial probes: 69 GPUI + 6 async, unchanged assertions, all pass;\n- fourth-round expected-behavior native groups: 20/20, plus CPU paint geometry and collection state/dependency probes;\n- async acceptance: 5/5, retaining explicit stale-callback rejection;\n- schema differential checks: 12,870 cases, no mismatch;\n- full workspace: 476 core tests plus integration/examples/CLI/registry; default contract: 446 tests; native suite: 134 tests, including active rotation suspension;\n- strict Clippy, rustdoc, structural performance, 69 visual baselines, package verification, artifact audit and macOS release smoke pass.\n\nOriginal audit reports and focused evidence are preserved; remediation and replay evidence are recorded alongside them. Publishing and tagging remain deferred for independent acceptance.\n","files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"USER_GUIDE.md","additions":21,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/app.rs","additions":127,"deletions":57,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/async_runtime.rs","additions":25,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/collection_projection.rs","additions":19,"deletions":22,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/column_resize.rs","additions":5,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/context.rs","additions":60,"deletions":21,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/effect.rs","additions":20,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/engine.rs","additions":253,"deletions":8,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/geometry.rs","additions":51,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/interaction.rs","additions":280,"deletions":29,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/lifecycle.rs","additions":174,"deletions":18,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/native_collection.rs","additions":104,"deletions":4,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/node.rs","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/pan_zoom.rs","additions":16,"deletions":10,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/primitive.rs","additions":64,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/range_slider.rs","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/renderer.rs","additions":60,"deletions":9,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/rotatable.rs","additions":44,"deletions":14,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/schema.rs","additions":312,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"crates/gpui-rhai/src/selectio